<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Cimpor 9-mth cons net up 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Cimpor 9-mth cons net up 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to Sept 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net  20.6 vs 14.7</p>
<p>Turnover 94.4 vs 88.2  </p>
<p>Operating profit 21.8 vs 24.3</p>
<p>Extraordinary profit 0.3 vs 0.8</p>
<p>Cash flow 33.4 vs 27.5</p>
<p>Financial profit 12.4 vs not available</p>
<p>NOTE: Company name is Cimpor-Cimentos de Portugal. &quot;The revaluation of the stake held in Banco de Fomento e Exterior (BFE), at a price of 2,615 escudos per share, the price at which the stake should be sold off in December 1996 in the public offer to buy BFE launched by Banco Portugues de Investimento, had a positive impact on the net profit results,&quot; Cimpor said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The growth in demand for cement in the first nine months helped push up accumulated sales, which stood 1.6 percent higher than in the same year-ago period,&quot; it added.</p>
</text>
